  "query_preview": "..Fri Nov 20 to Wed Nov 25...A few showers will linger\nin southwest San Diego County through Friday morning, before the\nweather dries and skies clear. Another shortwave trough rotates\nthrough the region on the east side of the larger trough Friday,\nbut this will mostly just keep us cooler than average. This is\nfollowed by a brief period of ridging Saturday, though this will\nbe weak and transient enough that temperatures will only bump up a\nfew degrees for Saturday afternoon. \n\nAnother weak shortwave follows late Sunday into Monday. This has a\nmoderate chance (~40% chance) of bringing some more precipitation\nto the region, though this would be much, much lighter. A handful\nof global ensemble members are still showing mostly dry weather,\nso confidence in the forecast for next week is moderate. Another\nbrief ridge is likely late Monday into Tuesday, before another low\npressure system looms towards late Tuesday-Wednesday. This latter\nsystem has trended slightly wetter, with more ensemble members\nshowing precipitation than previous runs, but there are large\ndifferences in strength, timing, and depth of troughing that will\nmake huge differences in the temperature, rain, etc. forecast for\nnext week.",
